{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415309-imitating-a-vampire","id":1415309,"title":"Imitating a Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-24T12:42:25-07:00","id":1415309,"title":"Imitating a Vampire","content":"If I wanted to pass for a vampire, at least in most cases, what would I need? <br /> <br /> I think Prime 2 / Mind 1 can be used to change my aura (make it look vampiric). But to make basic changes to my appearance is Life 3 enough or do I need Matter/Prime/something else to look convincingly &quot;corpse like&quot;. Also may need to alter &quot;scent&quot; a little bit, but not sure if needed or how.<br /> <br /> Obvious against a Tremere + Path of Blood this deception requires much more (possibly Prime 4 or 5 to make my Quintessence seem like vampire blood?) if it can be done.<br /> <br /> Thanks for any help or thoughts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T13:02:36-07:00","id":1415311,"title":"","content":"I'd say life 2 could alter your scent, matter 2 life 3 would be required to make your body look corpselike, or really good makeup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T13:06:28-07:00","id":1415312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Actual_Table</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1415309-imitating-a-vampire?p=1415311#post1415311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say life 2 could alter your scent, matter 2 life 3 would be required to make your body look corpselike, or really good makeup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Splash of entropy wouldn't hurt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T13:17:25-07:00","id":1415315,"title":"","content":"So maybe:<br /> <br /> **The Masquerade**<br /> Prime 3 Mind 3 Life 2 Matter 2 Entropy 1<br /> <br /> Appear as a Vampire through supernatural means, such as Auspex, and general perception, to someone with substantial experience identifying and/or being around vampires. <br /> <br /> <br /> Other thoughts:<br /> * Perhaps even add Forces 2 to remove reflection or something to mimic Lasombra curse? (Other clan curses could be mimicked other ways or just faked.) <br /> * You might also need to train yourself and/or alter something using Life 3 to drink human blood without gagging/puking. <br /> * Use Prime 5 Life 3 to turn your blood into &quot;potent blood&quot; that would seem vampiric by spending Quintessence per Blood Point consumed. This would hopefully be unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Also if you are using this to convince vampires that you are a vampire, would that be coincidental?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T13:51:52-07:00","id":1415322,"title":"","content":"No one has mentioned Spirit for a rote. Since an Avatar can be seen with Spirit and so can auras, I recommend Spirit 2 or higher in the rote. Probably also bump the Entropy in 'The Masquerade' up to rank 2, since that's when you can start doing a blessing for Life and other spheres so that adds manipulation. And you might need Forces 2 for the heat reduction.<br /> <br /> Honestly, unless dealing with vampires with exceptional senses, you might just go with Life and Mind.<br /> <br /> On the not gagging or puking on human blood, well, that's more a taste thing than a lack of a capacity to digest blood. So, no need for Life 3.<br /> <br /> You can probably find some more potent blood stuff in <i>Blood Treachery</i>, but remember that damns the Traditions.<br /> <br /> I'd call the magic vulgar without witnesses, since a human is not a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T20:03:50-07:00","id":1415646,"title":"","content":"The Back Door Parole rote in the <i>Orphan's Survival Guide</i> would allow you to fool most vampires, as it basically turns off all your signs of life while still allowing you to walk around. Mages have so many options for developing extra mystical senses though, it's really a matter of whom specifically you're trying to fool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T14:15:24-07:00","id":1415885,"title":"","content":"vampires often fake life-signs (blush of health, or obfuscate 3), you won't need to look corpse-like,<br /> <br /> ironically, on Camarilla territory, it might actually be an advantage to look human since they're enforcing the masqierade and all that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T15:04:40-07:00","id":1415890,"title":"","content":"Most vampires who are maintaining the Masquerade look pretty human to begin with. Just dress in Goth gear or 19th century clothes (or both lol) and you\u2019ll fool most vampires without even having to use magick. Prime 2 and Mind 2 should be enough to change your aura for vampires who use Auspex and higher levels of Prime and Life (maybe 3 each) should cloak you against vampires using blood sorcery to directly tell stuff about your Vitae (which ofc you don\u2019t have).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T10:05:08-07:00","id":1416008,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the great feedback on this. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3505_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3505\" data-vbnamecard=\"3505\">Matt the Bruins fan</a> - this is specifically to fool vampires. All the other PCs are vampires and I am trying to figure out how to blend in with them in kindred society. One of the PCs already has some merits (baby face, something that conceals his aura, and maybe something else) that hide the fact that he is a vampire pretty well and he has been pretending to be a ghoul of one of the other PCs. I have also been doing this and using Prime to conceal my aura although at least 1 vampire has seen it before I realized I should be doing that. I may have to kill that one. <br /> <br /> Also, this is in the Dark Ages, so I have more flexibility to do things without worrying about Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}